# Test / driver-contract-live-tier credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env.test` and fill in. `.env.test` is gitignored (`.gitignore`);
# this template is committed (negated by `!.env.test.example`) so it can never
# carry a real value.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How this is consumed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   scripts/run-live-contract.sh            # the driver contract live tier
#   scripts/run-live-contract.sh --dry-run  # resolve + report, run nothing
#
# The runner loads `.env`, then `.env.test`, then `packages/drivers/.env` if it
# exists — later wins. It *parses* KEY=VALUE rather than `source`-ing the file,
# because `source` executes whatever is in it and a parser can only assign.
#
# The tests themselves read the process environment ONLY (fake-runtime-fixtures
# §10.2 rule 5); they never open a file. That is deliberate — it keeps the
# credential source single and auditable.
#
# If you already keep a `postgres://…` or `mysql://…` URL in this file, the
# runner expands it into the TEST_* variables and you do not need section 1 or 2
# at all. `DATABASE_URL` is only accepted when its scheme names the family, so
# one shared URL cannot be handed to the wrong driver.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Safety rules the tests enforce, and why they exist
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These tests create, alter and DROP tables. They will not touch a database that
# is not obviously disposable:
#
#   TEST_*_DATABASE      MUST begin with `dz_fixture_`
#   TEST_*_DATABASE_B    MUST begin with `dz_fixture_`, and MUST differ from
#                        TEST_*_DATABASE. (If B is unset it defaults to A, and
#                        two equal targets are refused — the cross-database
#                        dimension would silently verify nothing.)
#   MIGRATION_TEST_DATABASE  MUST be exactly `datazen_test`, or start `dz_mig_`
#
# A refusal is a refusal, not a warning. Renaming a real database to
# `dz_fixture_…` to get past the check defeats the check; make a dedicated one:
#
#   createdb dz_fixture_pg_a && createdb dz_fixture_pg_b
#   mysql -e 'CREATE DATABASE dz_fixture_my_a; CREATE DATABASE dz_fixture_my_b;'
#
# The account also needs DDL rights (CREATE/ALTER/DROP), not just CONNECT.


# ===========================================================================
# 1. Driver contract live tier — PostgreSQL
# ===========================================================================
# Consumed by packages/drivers/postgres/tests/real_driver_contract.rs and
# postgres_cross_database.rs. Defaults, if omitted, come from the driver's own
# Contract: host 127.0.0.1, port 5432, user postgres.
#
#   TEST_PG_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   TEST_PG_PORT=5432
#   TEST_PG_USER=postgres
#   TEST_PG_PASSWORD=
TEST_PG_DATABASE=dz_fixture_pg_a
TEST_PG_DATABASE_B=dz_fixture_pg_b


# ===========================================================================
# 2. Driver contract live tier — MySQL
# ===========================================================================
# Consumed by packages/drivers/mysql/tests/real_driver_contract.rs and
# mysql_cross_database.rs. Defaults: host 127.0.0.1, port 3306, user root.
#
#   TEST_MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   TEST_MYSQL_PORT=3306
#   TEST_MYSQL_USER=root
#   TEST_MYSQL_PASSWORD=
TEST_MYSQL_DATABASE=dz_fixture_my_a
TEST_MYSQL_DATABASE_B=dz_fixture_my_b


# ===========================================================================
# 3. Strict mode — usually set for you
# ===========================================================================
# Unset, an unreachable server is a SKIP, and `test result: ok` cannot tell a
# skip from a pass. Set to 1 and an unverified dimension becomes a failure.
# scripts/run-live-contract.sh exports this for you; set it here only to make
# a bare `cargo test` strict too.
#
#   DATAZEN_CONTRACT_REQUIRE_LIVE=1


# ===========================================================================
# 4. Legacy `#[ignore]`d integration tests — postgres and mysql
# ===========================================================================
# These are opt-in and run with `--ignored`, and they are NOT part of the
# contract tier. They are separate integration suites with their own namespace.
# MIGRATION_TEST_DATABASE must be `datazen_test` or start with `dz_mig_`.
#
#   MIGRATION_TEST_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   MIGRATION_TEST_PORT=5432
#   MIGRATION_TEST_USER=postgres
#   MIGRATION_TEST_PASSWORD=
MIGRATION_TEST_DATABASE=


# ===========================================================================
# 5. Redis live tests
# ===========================================================================
# Also `#[ignore]`d, and gated on the URL being present at all.
#
#   DATAZEN_TEST_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
#   DATAZEN_TEST_REDIS_CLUSTER_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:7000
# Overrides the `redis-server` binary used by the in-process harness.
#   DATAZEN_REDIS_SERVER=/opt/homebrew/bin/redis-server


# ===========================================================================
# 6. Driver-internal unit tests
# ===========================================================================
# Not the contract tier — these are `#[cfg(test)]` tests inside the driver
# crates that reach for the vendor-standard libpq / MySQL variable names.
# Leaving these unset simply skips them.
#
#   PGHOST=127.0.0.1
#   PGPORT=5432
#   PGUSER=postgres
#   PGPASSWORD=
#   PGDATABASE=postgres
#
#   MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   MYSQL_PORT=3306
#   MYSQL_USER=root
#   MYSQL_PASSWORD=
#   MYSQL_DB=mysql
#
# Note: PGDATABASE / MYSQL_DB above are NOT read by run-live-contract.sh. The
# runner only borrows a bare vendor variable as a fallback when it can also
# name the database, so a half-filled block here cannot shadow section 1.


# ===========================================================================
# 7. SQL Server env-file opt-in
# ===========================================================================
# The SQL Server live tests may read their settings from a file. This variable
# names that file, and only a bare filename is accepted — a path is refused, so
# the opt-in cannot be widened into "read anything".
#
#   TEST_SQLSERVER_ENV_FILE=


# ===========================================================================
# 8. Escape hatch: names this template does not guess
# ===========================================================================
# If your env file spells these differently, do not edit this template. Put
# `YOUR_NAME = TEST_PG_NAME` lines in scripts/.live-contract.aliases (gitignored)
# and the runner will bind them. Keeping the mapping in a file rather than in
# the runner means nobody has to say their variable names out loud.
#
#   POSTGRES_USER = TEST_PG_USER
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD = TEST_PG_PASSWORD